.policy "ruff-f702-continue-outside-loop" revision 2
.description "Keep continue inside a for or while loop body; outside one (including a loop's else block) it is a Python syntax error."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff F702 (pyflakes): `continue` with no enclosing loop body in its own def, class or module. CPython rejects
// the file. A loop's `else` clause is not inside the loop, and a def or class in between hides an outer loop.
//   def f(): continue        ← F702
//   for x in xs: continue    not reported
#include "python/pyflakes.rr"
//   outside_loop(s)  break/continue s has no loop body around it in its def, class or module

.violation F702(at: node) code "F702" "`continue` not properly in loop"
    suppress ruff "F702"
F702(s) :- kind(s, "continue_statement"), outside_loop(s).
